# The story systems (dune_story_setup=comm): after Paul's first vision the
# Emperor's demand waits in the COMM room (palace room 8) and Duncan is there
# with 2000 kg in stock. VIEW NEW MESSAGES (second row) lists the sender;
# the Emperor's line; " Viewed"; then Duncan (fourth row) talks up to his
# offer and the bargaining menu (ds:1ffe); ACCEPT (second row) agrees and
# leaving the talk ships the spice (seg000:135ad, in the engine log).
#
# Comments after '#' on a command line say what a click hits and what a
# wait lets finish; scripts/dune_script_trace.py prints what each line did.
wait 15000              # the story setup loads and the COMM room draws
checkpoint story-comm-room
move 160 171
click left 160 171      # row 2: VIEW NEW MESSAGES: the list of senders
wait 1500               # the list shows
checkpoint story-comm-list
move 160 163
click left 160 163      # row 1: EMPEROR SHADDAM IV: “I want a shipment of 1060kgs of spice today!”
wait 1500               # the Emperor's message shows
checkpoint story-emperor
click left 160 80       # view: after his line, the row “ Viewed” comes up
wait 1000               # the row shows
move 160 163
click left 160 163      # row 1: “ Viewed”: the message closes
wait 1500               # back to the COMM room
move 160 187
click left 160 187      # row 4: Duncan IDAHO: “I must congratulate you on finding…”
wait 1500               # Duncan's first line shows
click left 160 80       # view: next line “Paul, I don't think that I've told you about the worms…”
wait 800                # the line shows
click left 160 80       # view: next line “Sandworms grow to enormous size…”
wait 800                # the line shows
click left 160 80       # view: next line “Don't hesitate to regroup your troops…”
wait 800                # the line shows
click left 160 80       # view: next line “Our stocks of spice are currently 2000 kgs”
wait 800                # the line shows
click left 160 80       # view: next line “The Emperor asked for a spice shipment, didn't he?”
wait 800                # the line shows
click left 160 80       # view: next line, his offer “We can send him what he asked for…” with the bargaining menu (ARGUE / ACCEPT / REFUSE) at once, as the original (action 4, seg000:a244)
wait 800                # the line and the menu show
checkpoint story-duncan-offer
click left 160 80       # view: a click on the view while the menu is up changes nothing (as the original, captures/menu-click)
wait 800                # the line and the menu stay
checkpoint story-bargain
move 160 171
click left 160 171      # row 2: ACCEPT: “Ok Paul, let's go to the communication room…”
wait 1500               # Duncan's answer shows
checkpoint story-accepted
click left 160 80       # view: next line “Come on, let's go to that communication room!”
wait 800                # the line shows
click left 160 80       # view, after the last line: closes the talk (the spice ships)
wait 800                # back to the COMM room
click left 160 80       # view: an empty spot (does nothing)
wait 800                # settle before quitting
quit
